**Fix getPort(config)**

`getPort(config)` should return `config.port`, or `3000` when the port is missing (`undefined` or `null`). Port `0` is valid and must be kept. Fix the bug.

```js
function getPort(config) {
  return config.port || 3000;
}
```

notes.back:
// Why: `||` replaces every falsy value, 0 included; `??` replaces only null and undefined.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Nullish_coalescing
function getPort(config) {
  return config.port ?? 3000;
}

